/target
/xtask/target
/crates/dstu-core/fuzz/target
/crates/dstu-core/fuzz/corpus
/crates/dstu-core/fuzz/artifacts
**/*.rs.bk
/xtask/Cargo.lock
/crates/dstu-core/fuzz/Cargo.lock
*.pdb
.claude.local.md
/.claude/

# DSTU 9041:2020 primary standard text - purchased/library-scanned copy (5,304 UAH,
# fnd-store.uas.gov.ua, per docs/ORACLES.md), unlike the freely available DSTU_4145-2002.pdf scan
# already tracked above it in docs/papers/. Kept locally as the primary source for hazmat::dstu9041
# (T-46), never committed - state-standard text redistribution rights are not ours to grant.
/docs/papers/DSTU_9041-2020.pdf
# OCR transcript derived from the file above (Surya OCR, spot-checked against PaddleOCR,
# 2026-08-04) - same redistribution restriction applies to a transcript of the text as to the
# scan itself, so this stays local too. See the file's own header for the OCR methodology and
# its `[OCR-СУМНІВНО]` uncertainty markers - a best-effort transcript, not a verified oracle.
/docs/papers/DSTU_9041-2020_ocr.md
# Supplementary purchased pages (2026-08-05, National Library of Ukraine EDD service) filling
# specific gaps in the scan above - clauses 6.5-6.12, the rest of section 3, Додаток А/Б/Д. Same
# redistribution restriction as the main scan/transcript above, same reason.
/docs/papers/DSTU_9041-2020_supplement.pdf
/docs/papers/DSTU_9041-2020_supplement_ocr.md
# A redacted excerpt (signatures/official markings stripped) of the same purchased text above -
# stripping the letterhead does not strip copyright over the substantive clause text it still
# reproduces, so the same redistribution restriction applies. Never committed either.
/docs/papers/DSTU_9041-2020_Part of.pdf

# Oracle-harness build artifacts and fetched dependencies (Java/.NET) — fetched fresh via
# Maven/NuGet at build time (see tests/oracle-harness/*/README or docs/TASKS.md "Infrastructure"),
# never vendored or committed, same rule as /oracles below.
/tests/oracle-harness/java/lib/
/tests/oracle-harness/java/out/
/tests/oracle-harness/java/target/
/tests/oracle-harness/dotnet/bin/
/tests/oracle-harness/dotnet/obj/
# Compiled C oracle-harness drivers (gcc output built ad hoc per the build command in each .c
# file's own doc comment, never checked in) - same convention as the two rules above.
/tests/oracle-harness/*/*.exe
/tests/oracle-harness/*/*.o
# uapki-cmac-bench (T-133/D-83) links against UAPKI's prebuilt DLL, downloaded fresh per its own
# build recipe, not vendored - the DLL itself and the gendef/dlltool-generated import lib are
# local build products, same as the .exe above.
/tests/oracle-harness/uapki-cmac-bench/*.dll
/tests/oracle-harness/uapki-cmac-bench/*.def
/tests/oracle-harness/uapki-cmac-bench/*.a

# Third-party reference implementations, used only as oracles for local test-vector
# cross-verification (see oracles/README.md, docs/DECISIONS.md D-02/D-06). Never vendored into
# crates/, never committed or published — regardless of the upstream license.
# oracles/README.md itself stays tracked so the reasoning survives a fresh clone.
/oracles/*
!/oracles/README.md

# firmware/qemu-stm32-smoketest (T-170, D-156): its own separate Cargo workspace, same reason as
# the bindings below - the root-scoped /target rule doesn't reach it.
/firmware/*/target/

# Language bindings (docs/bindings-strategy.md, D-119): each is its own separate Cargo workspace,
# so the root-scoped /target rule above doesn't reach its build output - and each has its own
# language-ecosystem build/cache artifacts on top of that. Cargo.lock IS committed per binding
# (same reproducible-build reasoning as the root Cargo.lock, which is tracked for `uacrypt`).
/bindings/*/target/
/bindings/python/__pycache__/
/bindings/python/**/__pycache__/
/bindings/python/.venv/
/bindings/python/dist/
/bindings/python/*.egg-info/
/bindings/python/.pytest_cache/
# `maturin develop`'s editable-install artifact: the compiled extension copied straight into the
# python-source tree (platform-specific binary, `*.pyd` on Windows/`*.so` on Linux/macOS).
/bindings/python/python/dstu_core/*.pyd
/bindings/python/python/dstu_core/*.so

# Node.js (T-50): node_modules (fetched fresh via `npm install`, never vendored, same rule as
# `/oracles` above), plus napi-rs's own build output under native/ - the compiled addon (`*.node`,
# platform-specific binary, same class as Python's `.pyd`/`.so` above) and `index.js`/`index.d.ts`,
# both fully generated from this crate's `#[napi]` annotations by `napi build native` (T-50 step 3
# - relocated out of the package root so the hand-written idiomatic `js/index.js` wrapper,
# `secretstream.js`'s stream.Transform pair, D-118, could live at the package root instead) -
# regenerated every build rather than committed, so there is no separate copy of the low-level
# binding surface that can drift out of sync with the Rust source of truth.
/bindings/nodejs/node_modules/
/bindings/nodejs/native/
/bindings/nodejs/npm/

# Ruby (T-160): rake-compiler's own staging/build dirs, plus the compiled extension copied into
# lib/dstu_core/ (rake's own `copy` task target - platform-specific binary, same class as Python's
# `.so`/Node's `.node` above), regenerated every `rake compile`. `pkg/` is `rake native gem`'s own
# output directory (the precompiled, platform-tagged .gem, D-136) - rebuilt per release, not vendored.
/bindings/ruby/tmp/
/bindings/ruby/pkg/
/bindings/ruby/lib/dstu_core/*.so
/bindings/ruby/.bundle/
/bindings/ruby/*.gem

# PHP (T-159): PHPUnit ships as a standalone PHAR (D-145 - no Composer dependency added just for a
# test runner), downloaded per-machine/CI rather than vendored.
/bindings/php/phpunit.phar
/bindings/php/.phpunit.result.cache
# PHPStan (T-208): same standalone-PHAR-no-Composer posture as phpunit.phar above.
/bindings/php/phpstan.phar

# .NET (T-52): standard MSBuild output dirs per project, `dotnet pack`'s own output, plus the
# local NuGet feed step 4's fresh-install check publishes into (D-116 - build/local-install only,
# no registry publish).
/bindings/dotnet/*/bin/
/bindings/dotnet/*/obj/
/bindings/dotnet/*/nupkg/
/bindings/dotnet/local-nuget-feed/

# Java (T-51): the Rust JNI crate lives nested under bindings/java/native/ (not bindings/java
# itself, to avoid colliding with Maven's own src/main/java layout) - the root-scoped
# /bindings/*/target/ rule below only reaches one path segment deep, so this crate's own build
# output needs its own explicit entry. /bindings/java/target/ is Maven's own output (already
# covered by /bindings/*/target/, listed again here just for locality with the rest of this
# section) plus this binding's own compiled examples/ output.
/bindings/java/native/target/
/bindings/java/target/

# C++ (T-53): header-only, no Rust glue of its own - just CMake's own out-of-tree build directory
# (compiled test/example binaries, copied-in dstu_core_capi shared library, CMakeCache.txt).
/bindings/cpp/build/
# Separate CMake tree cpp-tidy/cpp-cppcheck configure into for their own compile_commands.json
# (T-208) - kept apart from /build above so a plain `cargo xtask cpp` never touches it.
/bindings/cpp/build-tidy/
